  "content": {
    "id": "p3-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "For any non-right-angled $\\triangle ABC$, prove that\n$$\\tan A+\\tan B+\\tan C=\\tan A\\cdot\\tan B\\cdot\\tan C.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Proved using $A+B=\\pi-C$ and the tangent addition formula.",
      "worked": "Since $A+B+C=\\pi$, we have $\\tan C=-\\tan(A+B)$. Hence\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\tan A+\\tan B+\\tan C&=\\tan A+\\tan B-\\tan(A+B)\\\\\n\\tan A+\\tan B+\\tan C&=\\frac{(\\tan A+\\tan B)(1-\\tan A\\tan B)-(\\tan A+\\tan B)}{1-\\tan A\\tan B}\\\\\n\\tan A+\\tan B+\\tan C&=-\\tan A\\tan B\\frac{\\tan A+\\tan B}{1-\\tan A\\tan B}\\\\\n\\tan A+\\tan B+\\tan C&=-\\tan A\\tan B\\tan(A+B)\\\\\n\\tan A+\\tan B+\\tan C&=\\tan A\\tan B\\tan C.\n\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 65
  },
